## 10. Key Differences from Dynamic-Indexer

| Aspect | Dynamic-Indexer | Legacy-Sync |
|--------|-----------------|-------------|
| **Data Sink** | Elasticsearch (bulk indexing) | Legacy HTTP API (queue push) |
| **Sync Mechanism** | Write to ES index | HTTP POST/PUT/DELETE to external service |
| **Product Categorization** | Single index | Linked vs Unlinked vs Delete |
| **Output Ports** | IndexRepository | LegacyReserveSyncRepository |
| **Service Endpoints** | ES REST API | Legacy API `/pushQueue.json` |
| **HTTP Methods** | PUT/POST (bulk) | Explicit POST/PUT/DELETE per operation |
| **Response Handling** | Bulk response parsing | Simple success/failure check |
| **Timeout** | Larger (depends on bulk size) | 500ms (small payloads) |
| **Use Case** | Real-time search indexing | Legacy system synchronization |

