## 11. Key Patterns & Design Decisions

### 11.1 Suspend Functions & Coroutines
- All repository methods are `suspend` functions
- Enables non-blocking async HTTP calls via WebFlux
- `runBlocking` in application service bridges blocking Kafka listener to async operations
- `supervisorScope` prevents cascading failures

### 11.2 Product Categorization Strategy
```kotlin
when {
    data.isCatalogMatch -> { linked.add(...) }
    op == Operation.DELETE -> { unlinkedDeletes.add(...) }
    else -> { unlinked.add(...) }
}
```
- Catalog-matched products prioritized
- Delete operations routed to special endpoint
- CREATE/UPDATE for non-matched products use standard path

### 11.3 Dependency Resolution
- Extract all unique IDs from batch
- Fetch from cache in parallel (CompletableFuture)
- Enrich before mapping to legacy DTOs
- Fallbacks for missing references (empty strings, 0 values)

### 11.4 Error Isolation
- `supervisorScope` prevents one failed push from blocking others
- Individual push failures logged but don't block acknowledgment
- Kafka offset NOT committed on listener exception
- Silent continuation within supervisorScope (onFailure handler)

### 11.5 Conditional Component Registration
```kotlin
@ConditionalOnProperty(name = ["legacy-sync.enabled"], havingValue = "true")
```
- Same bootstrap can run only legacy-sync (index.enabled: false, dynamic-indexer.enabled: false)
- Prevents resource conflicts and simplifies deployment

